      "type": "text",
      "value": "Write down the complex form of Fourier series. Find a series of sine and cosine multiple of x which represent $x + x ^ { 2 }$ in the interval $- \\pi < x < \\pi$ and hence deduce that,"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "value": "$$\n\\begin{array} { r } { { \\frac { \\pi ^ { 2 } } { 6 } } = \\sum _ { n = 1 } ^ { \\infty } { \\frac { 1 } { n ^ { 2 } } } . } \\end{array}\n$$",
      "format": "latex"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "value": "$$\n\\begin{array} { r } { \\frac { 1 } { 1 ^ { 2 } . 3 ^ { 2 } } + \\frac { 1 } { 3 ^ { 2 } . 5 ^ { 2 } } + \\frac { 1 } { 5 ^ { 2 } . 7 ^ { 2 } } + \\cdots = \\frac { \\pi ^ { 2 } - 8 } { 1 6 } . } \\end{array}\n$$",
